WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.430
Speaker 1: Let's go to the phone lines.

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:05.740
We do that via Discord at David Pakman dot
com slash discord.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.490
I want to start today.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.440
Let's go to and from eastern Iowa and you're
on the air.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.440
What's on your mind, my friend?

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.800
Speaker 2: Hi, do I sound OK, Andy?

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.109
Speaker 1: You sound absolutely perfect.

00:00:18.109 --> 00:00:19.880
Speaker 2: Awesome.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.230
Got a real quick one for you!

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:28.090
What do you think is the first like steps
for younger people getting into politics to

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.099
kind of get more involved
Speaker 1: even before maybe they're old enough

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:33.610
to actually run for something, you mean?

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:34.610
Yes.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.010
Get on, get involved in a campaign.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.989
And when I say a campaign, it doesn't have
to be a candidate campaign.

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:41.710
It could even be an issue based campaign.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:47.899
It could be maybe the city council where you
are wants to bring municipal broadband.

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:49.420
Get involved in advocating for that.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.859
If it's going to be, it's going to be a voter
initiative, a ballot initiative or whatever.

00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:58.790
Just get involved in something you can help
on campaigns in most places.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.109
There's no age limit.

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:02.109
Find something you care about.

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:03.180
Maybe it's a candidate.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.060
Maybe it's an issue and just jump in and get
involved.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.450
All right.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:08.840
Thank you.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:09.840
My pleasure.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.220
All right, Andy, from eastern Iowa, very much
appreciate that

